POST /api/support with {email, message: 'Name: … / Company: … / text', type: kind, page, lang}. The route:
- allows 10 per IP per hour (429 slow_down);
- requires email and message (400);
- records the login and the account when a session exists;
- pushes the ticket with status 'open' onto support-tickets (capped at 2000);
- emails WAITLIST_TO when it is set (sendEmail sends nothing without RESEND_API_KEY, and a send that gets no answer in 10 seconds counts as not sent).
The founder reads enterprise and early-adopter tickets in the console's Leads tab (GET /api/admin/leads, isAdmin; the 'all' view adds every other ticket) or through GET /api/support (isAdmin). No route updates a ticket, and nothing is sent to the person.
